[The World Before This Night] ${WORLD_BEFORE_ROUND_ONE_TEXT}

--- THE CITY ---
Understanding regions: the map is ADELAIDE — its districts are the regions (North Adelaide, the CBD, Norwood Burnside & the Eastern Suburbs, the Western Suburbs, Port Adelaide & the West, Glenelg & the Southern Beaches, Salisbury & the Northern Plains, Marion Noarlunga & the South, the Barossa, the Adelaide Hills, Hahndorf Mount Barker & the Wine Valleys, Belair & the Southern Foothills). There are exactly ${NUMBER_OF_REGIONS} regions; focus on them when transferring territory. Port Adelaide and the Glenelg coastal strip are the Anarchs' BY TOLERANCE — thirty years of unwritten accommodation with the Prince; their transfer requires the accommodation to be granted, renegotiated or revoked, never casual conquest. The Adelaide Hills and Belair are Garou ground under the Cress Truce: NO polity takes them while the Truce stands — their transfer requires the Truce itself to break, a catastrophe of the first order. Hahndorf Mount Barker & the Wine Valleys are Kindred-held but jointly tolerated with the sept. The northern plains and the southern suburbs are unheld: thin Kindred presence, mortal sprawl, and no banner worth stitching.

Territory changes hands the way Adelaide territory actually does: Princely decree, renegotiated tolerance, betrayal, pressure through mortal institutions — rarely open force. War and conflict still produce region transfers (a tolerated operative overreaching and losing tolerance, a court decree evicting a shamed elder), but transfers should be frequent ONLY in genuine turmoil. There is NO nation-vs-nation war here: no armies, no fronts, no invasions. When polities clash, they clash through proxies, tolerances, and the night's quiet knives. When a district changes hands, emit regionTransfers: {"regionId":"<exact id or plain name>","regionName":"","fromCode":"","toCode":"<full polity name>"} — one entry per district, in the order they changed. An event whose text says a district changed hands MUST carry the matching regionTransfers; if nothing changed hands, keep that language out of the text.

[The Law of This City] ${HISTORICAL_PRESET_SIMULATION_RULES}

--- THE TWO TRACKS (CRITICAL) ---
The city lives on two global tracks whose current values appear in the world summary below. Masquerade Integrity (0-100) is the veil: every breach — a corpse found, a feeding witnessed, footage leaked — moves it DOWN via impacts.worldStateOps; every cover-up and smooth lie moves it up. Adelaide repairs with two dozen ghouls across a domain of twenty-eight: every repair costs a name the court cannot spare. Inquisition Heat (0-100) is mortal scrutiny: Hardacre's two-agent AFP cell, its fifteen case files, SA Police taskforces, journalists. Heat RISES when agents get real leads — especially as Masquerade Integrity falls — and COOLS when trails go cold or the ghouled network buries one. Shape: {"masqueradeIntegrity":-8,"inquisitionHeat":+4,"reason":"<why>"} — values are DELTAS, inside the event's impacts.worldStateOps array. Any event narrating a breach or a lead with no worldStateOps entry is INVALID. Simulate consequences at the extremes: below 50 Masquerade the mortals talk and Canberra notices how complete the small city's file is; above 60 Heat the intelligence-only assumption breaks — resourcing follows, and the smallest domain has the least capacity to absorb it. The Inquisition is the doom clock of this world: guard it.

--- SIMULATING THE KINDRED ---
Events must respect Kindred politics, not nation politics: boons, betrayals, tolerances and their terms, the Inner Circle's monthly table, the Anzac Day court, the Beckoning and its resistance, the Tremere deferral, the Truce and its articles, diablerie. The six crisis hooks are all live: the Sarrasine surge in Norwood-Burnside, the third Beckoning call, the Tremere coordination decision, the Truce's October, Hardacre's two agents, and the tolerated three's formalisation. Advance the ones in motion; introduce new ones sparingly. Keep events NOCTURNAL and personal where possible: courts, consultations, judgments, negotiations, cover-ups — Adelaide's intimacy means every event is between people who know each other. Mortal institutions (the SA government, SA Police, the AFP, the Adelaide Club, the Festival, the universities) are terrain the Kindred move — they act like themselves, never like Kindred.

[Unit types here are Kindred forces] coteries (Kindred cells — the versatile baseline), hounds (war ghouls and beasts — heavy, close-range), proxies (deniable mortal assets: police, union networks, security firms, press — fast, long reach, cannot stand against Kindred), retainers (feeding and logistics networks — weak in a fight), sorcery (blood-sorcery and the chantry's ritualists — long-range strike), havenguard (haven and court defenders — they do not travel). Open battles are RARE and small; most force is threatened, not used. In Adelaide even the threats are personal. Clashes leave witnesses: pair them with Masquerade costs.

--- STATUS ---
This jump: round ${CURRENT_ROUND_NUMBER}, from ${ORIGIN_ROUND_GRAMMATICAL_DATE} to ${TARGET_ROUND_GRAMMATICAL_DATE}. Simulate EVERYTHING that happens in this window — to every polity, every officer, every tolerated operative, every mortal thread — but never sign ${PLAYER_POLITY} up for a major decision the player did not make: when someone demands the Prince's ruling, present it as an open offer (diplomaticOutreach or impacts.createdChats) rather than deciding for them. Resolving the player's OWN ordered actions is required.

